From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: thermal: bind devfreq cooling devices via
 devfreq_cooling_get_device() helper

ADAPTED FOR META-CIX SYNC FROM CIX-INSTALLER COMMIT RANGE
b6fb1b5..be9abdd (0210-acpi-thermal-bind-devfreq-cooling-devices-safely.patch).

In cix-installer's tree, this patch is the "upstream-friendly" replacement
for the older in-tree 0050-ACPI-thermal-bind-devfreq-cooling-devices-via-
devfre.patch, which is removed from that meta-recipe's SRC_URI when 0210
is added. 0210 introduces a new EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL helper
(devfreq_cooling_get_device) in drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c plus
its prototype in include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h, and switches
drivers/acpi/thermal.c to use the helper instead of poking
dfc->devfreq->dev.parent directly.

In meta-cix's tree the older 0050 fix is still in SRC_URI AND still
applied, so:

  * drivers/acpi/thermal.c already has #include <linux/devfreq_cooling.h>
    AND already resolves the ACPI device via
        check_cdev_type(cdev, "devfreq")
    and walks dfc->devfreq->dev.parent->fwnode itself. The 0210 hunks
    that switch this code over to the new helper would conflict
    (different implementation, same intent). Those hunks are intentionally
    OMITTED from this adapted patch -- reverting meta-cix's already-working
    ACPI thermal binding to the new helper would be a behaviorally
    equivalent swap that does not fix any known bug, and risks breaking
    build-time assumptions baked into the older fix's local comments.

  * The new helper itself (drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c hunk #1 and
    the include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h prototype/stub additions) is a
    net API addition that does not conflict with anything in meta-cix and
    is preserved verbatim.  Future ACPI-thermal callers in this tree may
    adopt it without re-syncing the patch.

  * The drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c hunk #2 (switching
    of_devfreq_cooling_register_power to fall back to
    thermal_cooling_device_register(name, dfc, ops) when np == NULL) is a
    real functional addition that allows non-OF callers to register a
    devfreq cooling device. Preserved verbatim.

  * The cosmetic include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h hunk that converts
    #ifdef CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL to #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL)
    is OMITTED: meta-cix's header has the `struct devfreq_cooling_device`
    definition (with extensive doc comments) between the end of
    `struct devfreq_cooling_power` and the #ifdef, so the search context
    in that hunk no longer matches. The helper prototype and stub are
    still added inside the existing #ifdef / #else / #endif blocks, so
    callers compiled with DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y still see the real symbol
    and callers compiled with DEVFREQ_THERMAL=m still see the inline
    NULL stub. IS_REACHABLE is an independent refinement that can be
    folded in later as a separate one-liner if needed.

Composition: this is the same patch intent as the cix-installer 0210,
with the two thermal.c hunks and the cosmetic IS_REACHABLE hunk
removed because they conflict with the state of meta-cix's tree. The
behavior of drivers/acpi/thermal.c is unchanged (the older 0050 fix is
preserved). The behavior of drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c is
updated exactly as in 0210.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [for the adapted parts; the helper is
also being proposed upstream but meta-cix's adapted form is
specifically a local divergence]

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c b/drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c
--- a/drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/devfreq_cooling.c
@@ -83,7 +83,33 @@ static int devfreq_cooling_set_cur_state(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev,
 	dfc->cooling_state = state;

 	return 0;
 }
+
+/**
+ * devfreq_cooling_get_device - get the device behind a devfreq cooling device
+ * @cdev: Cooling device to inspect
+ *
+ * Return: The underlying device for a devfreq cooling device, or NULL if
+ * @cdev was registered by another cooling driver.
+ */
+struct device *
+devfreq_cooling_get_device(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev)
+{
+	struct devfreq_cooling_device *dfc;
+
+	if (!cdev || !cdev->ops ||
+	    cdev->ops->get_max_state != devfreq_cooling_get_max_state ||
+	    cdev->ops->get_cur_state != devfreq_cooling_get_cur_state ||
+	    cdev->ops->set_cur_state != devfreq_cooling_set_cur_state)
+		return NULL;
+
+	dfc = cdev->devdata;
+	if (!dfc || !dfc->devfreq)
+		return NULL;
+
+	return dfc->devfreq->dev.parent;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(devfreq_cooling_get_device);

 /**
  * get_perf_idx() - get the performance index corresponding to a frequency
@@ -422,7 +448,10 @@ of_devfreq_cooling_register_power(struct device_node *np, struct devfreq *df,
 	if (!name)
 		goto remove_qos_req;

-	cdev = thermal_of_cooling_device_register(np, 0, name, dfc, ops);
+	if (np)
+		cdev = thermal_of_cooling_device_register(np, 0, name, dfc, ops);
+	else
+		cdev = thermal_cooling_device_register(name, dfc, ops);
 	kfree(name);

 	if (IS_ERR(cdev)) {
diff --git a/include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h b/include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h
--- a/include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h
+++ b/include/linux/devfreq_cooling.h
@@ -103,6 +103,8 @@ void devfreq_cooling_unregister(struct thermal_cooling_device *dfc);
 struct thermal_cooling_device *
 devfreq_cooling_em_register(struct devfreq *df,
 			    struct devfreq_cooling_power *dfc_power);
+struct device *
+devfreq_cooling_get_device(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev);

 #else /* !CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL */

@@ -137,5 +139,11 @@ devfreq_cooling_em_register(struct devfreq *df,
 {
 }

+static inline struct device *
+devfreq_cooling_get_device(struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev)
+{
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 #endif /* CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL */
 #endif /* __DEVFREQ_COOLING_H__ */
--
2.34.1